  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 13-layer planar multilayer film on aluminum substrate for spectral selectivity. Stack sequence from air incident side: hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), Cr (Rakic-LD), hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), then Al (Rakic-LD) substrate. All 13 film layer thicknesses are design variables. Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm (maximize absorptance, minimize reflectance), 700-2000 nm (maximize reflectance). Incidence: normal, unpolarized. Thickness bounds: lower bound 8.0 nm (hard clamp to prevent TMM singularity), upper bound expanded by 20% from prior round (approximately 360 nm for dielectrics, 60 nm for Cr (Rakic-LD)). Initialize optimization using the thickness vector from iteration 10's best candidate (target_score 0.6506025858694148): [123.34, 168.22, 10.99, 124.58, 66.98, 108.29, 110.57, 54.71, 76.87, 128.36, 69.57, 139.84, 98.00] nm, with Gaussian perturbations scaled to 5% of the relaxed bounds. Use coherent TMM solver. Score both wavelength bands simultaneously to prevent trade-off sacrifice.",
